I am pleased to submit my manuscript entitled “Aetheris: A Multi‑Scale Integrated Simulation Framework for Unified Astrophysical, Mechanobiological, and Molecular Dynamics Modeling” for consideration in Nature Computational Science.

This work introduces Aetheris, a unified simulation architecture capable of synchronizing astrophysical fluid dynamics, cellular mechanobiology, and molecular dynamics within a single computational framework. The system integrates three traditionally isolated scientific domains through a Unified Memory Fabric (U.M.F.), enabling cross‑scale data exchange, temporal harmonization, and emergent behavior detection across macro‑, meso‑, and micro‑scale regimes.

The manuscript presents:

the mathematical foundations of each module,

the computational architecture enabling multi‑scale coupling,

the validation pathway demonstrating module‑level and cross‑scale consistency,

the high‑performance deployment strategy, and

the scientific implications of a unified multi‑scale simulation environment.

Aetheris does not propose new physical laws; instead, it provides a framework that allows existing physics, biology, and chemistry models to interact coherently across scales. This architecture enables forms of interdisciplinary simulation that have not previously been computationally feasible and may support new avenues of research in astrophysics, mechanobiology, molecular science, and computational physics.

I confirm that this manuscript is original, has not been published elsewhere, and is not under consideration by any other journal. All data sources, equations, and computational methods are fully documented.

Thank you for considering this submission. I welcome peer review and evaluation from your editorial board and reviewers.

